course: dictionary
lesson: 7175
title: Persecution: unfair treatment
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Persecution is a hard word, but its context gives you clues. It means cruel and unfair treatment of a person or group, often because of their religion, race, beliefs or who they are. «Refugees are people forced to flee their homes because of war or persecution.» Flee means run away, so these people run away from danger because they are being hunted or hurt.
explain: Look at the words around it. Forced, flee and hunted all point to danger and unfairness. Ask yourself: is someone being treated badly just for who they are or what they believe? If yes, persecution is probably the right meaning.
explain: Persecution is a noun, so it names a thing. You will see it in phrases such as «religious persecution», «suffer persecution» and «face persecution». Each phrase tells you that a person or group is being treated this way.
fact: Persecution means cruel and unfair treatment of a person or group.
fact: «Religious persecution» means being treated cruelly because of your religion.
fact: «Flee persecution» means to run away from cruel and unfair treatment.
fact: In history, some Roman emperors persecuted the early Christians.
fact: Persecution is uncountable, so you do not usually say «a persecution» for the idea itself; «persecutions» is used only when you mean several separate cases.
exercise: «Refugees are people forced to flee their homes because of war or persecution.» What does persecution mean? | A kind and friendly way of helping others | Moving house for a new job | *Cruel and unfair treatment of people for who they are | A long journey on a ship
exercise: In history, some Roman emperors caused the persecution of early Christians. What does this mean? | Christians wrote a new book together | Christians were given free land by the emperors | *Christians were treated cruelly and unfairly for their beliefs | Christians were invited to a big feast
exercise: The phrase «religious persecution» tells you why the treatment happens. Which word tells you why? | Cruel | History | *Religious | Flee
test: Which phrase means to run away from cruel and unfair treatment? | *Flee persecution | Religious persecution | Face a long walk | Suffer persecution
test: Why might people be persecuted? | Because they like to read books | *Because of their religion, race, beliefs or who they are | Because they have a birthday | Because it is raining
exam: Which sentence uses the word persecution correctly? | She ran quickly to persecution at the bus stop | The dog had persecution in its bowl | *Her family had to flee their town because of religious persecution | The persecution was a tasty cake for tea
